WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.470
- So I've played a lot
of video games in my day,

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:06.230
whether I'm playing Fallout
or The Sims or RuneScape,

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:08.660
just to clarify, I don't
still play RuneScape.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.190
I've noticed there's a commonality

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:11.650
to pretty much every game

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:15.120
and that's this idea that when
you upgrade your character,

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.550
your traits and your skills,

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.550
you get to unlock new
abilities, new opportunities,

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.580
travel to new parts of the
map and wield better stuff.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.060
You know, in RuneScape, if
you wanna wear rune armor,

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.780
you gotta grind it out,
fight like a billion goblins

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:32.750
or guards and grind your
defense level to level 40.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.600
In the Sims, if you wanna
make any money whatsoever,

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.010
you gotta pick a skill, max it out,

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.510
and then you can start making money.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:40.760
And in Fallout, New Vegas,

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.510
if you try to make it to
New Vegas before you upgrade

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.400
your character and your stats
and your perks and stuff,

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.970
you're gonna get completely
manhandled by a flying bug.

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:51.730
Even though this is kind
of a shower thought,

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:54.550
it really got me thinking
about how life kind of works

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.330
in the exact same way.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:59.700
By upgrading your skills,
developing your talents,

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.480
acquiring positive personality traits,

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.440
it really opens up a lot of
new opportunities in life.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.320
You get to travel to new parts of the map

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.750
and you start making more money

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:10.450
and you get to wield better stuff.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:12.070
And although this is pretty obvious,

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:15.500
I feel like we as human beings
forget about this a lot.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.290
We focus a ton on outcomes.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:20.040
We wanna pay off our student loans,

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.400
or we wanna get a girlfriend,
or we wanna move out

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.160
of our crappy apartment
into a nicer part of town.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:28.560
We get very caught up in all
the good things we want to have

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.920
happen to us, completely ignoring the fact

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:33.470
that some sort of personal transformation

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:35.890
likely needs to happen
in order for these things

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:37.020
to actually happen,

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.540
or at least have a higher
likelihood of happening.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.120
We're always tempted to
look outside of ourselves

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.450
for the solutions to our
problems, but we forget that

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:49.540
often our situation is just
a symptom of our character,

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.270
the character we're playing as.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:54.340
Our ever-growing debt
is often just a symptom

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:57.750
of our bad spending habits
and our inability as a person

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.360
to delay gratification.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:02.410
Our lack of friends might be a symptom

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:05.240
of our lack of confidence
and low self-esteem,

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:06.880
but we don't like to realize that.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:09.560
We don't like to admit
that maybe we're the ones

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:10.670
that need working on.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:12.170
Imagine going to the doctor one day,

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:15.360
because you wake up, your
whole body's in pain.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.340
Maybe you have a history of,
I don't know, a bone disease

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:19.400
or something in your family,

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.280
and you're really concerned and scared.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.530
So you go to the doctor
looking for answers

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:26.387
and the doctor's like, "Hmm, pain, right?

00:02:26.387 --> 00:02:27.810
"Here, have some painkillers."

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:29.550
You consider him a pretty crappy doctor

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.670
because he's not actually
trying to investigate

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:33.790
what the root cause of the issue is.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:35.230
He's just treating the symptom,

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:38.020
but that's exactly how
we often treat ourselves

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:39.280
and our own problems.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.000
It's like standing at the shore,

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:44.010
trying to push the waves
away and prevent them

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.930
from hitting the shore with your hands,

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.490
it's just so futile.

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:49.090
You might stop a couple of them,

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:50.940
but the waves are just
gonna keep on coming.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:54.620
All of this to say one simple
idea, that's really helped me

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:58.100
trend my life in an upward
direction is to focus

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:01.870
on internal improvement rather
than external improvement.

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:04.490
Instead of shopping for
a sexy new wardrobe,

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:07.740
that'll make me feel more
confident and give me a little

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:11.320
bit of swagger in my step,
I stop myself and I think,

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:14.140
what's something I can work on
internally that will help me

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:15.860
achieve the exact same goal?

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:18.130
You know, how can I feel
confident without having

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.060
to buy something or get something?

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.260
Usually that means getting off my butt

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.080
and developing more discipline at the gym,

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.640
having a great workout,
starting to eat better.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.110
These are things that'll help me feel

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:31.360
a sense of accomplishment
and make me feel proud

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:34.560
of who I am, which will make
me feel a lot more confident

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.190
than a new shirt ever could.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:39.640
Or if I'm feeling like my
videos aren't cinematic enough

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:41.450
and I'm really tempted to pull the trigger

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:44.340
on a really expensive
cinema camera on B&amp;H,

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.450
I stop myself and think about
what's something I can work on

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:50.880
internally that will help
me achieve that cinema look?

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.680
Well, the answer's pretty obvious.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:55.620
Maybe I should learn how
to light things better,

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:58.300
frame things better,
work on my composition.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.670
Upgrading my skills as a filmmaker

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:04.260
will do a lot more to improve
myself as a filmmaker,

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:05.830
than buying a new camera.

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:08.040
Usually the best answers to our problems

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:10.920
lie within ourselves and
they're really unexciting

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.990
and they're not as stimulating
as buying something

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:15.270
or getting something, but
they're the actual way

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:16.470
to solve the problem.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:19.130
And the nice thing about
focusing on internal improvement

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.240
rather than external
improvement is that you develop

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:25.160
a sort of resiliency to the chaos of life,

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:28.520
because truth is anything
that you get or attain

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:30.630
or any external upgrade you can make,

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:32.970
can be taken away from you
in the blink of an eye,

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:35.730
whether that's a pandemic
sweeping the nation and you end up

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:38.550
losing a job that you
worked really hard to get,

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:41.610
or maybe the economy
crashes and you lose all the

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:43.250
investments that you made

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:46.030
and if you spent all your
time putting your eggs

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:50.390
in the external basket, and
it all goes away overnight,

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.000
then you're left with pretty much nothing.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.270
But if you spent your time
investing in yourself internally,

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:58.060
then if you lose all the things
you've worked on externally,

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:01.260
you've developed the character
to bounce back from chaos.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.580
You've developed skills
that makes you valuable

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:06.400
to your community and
your family and yourself.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:08.290
You can make something out of nothing

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:12.390
and you can be somebody who
naturally creates good outcomes,

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:14.840
rather than somebody who's
just focusing on changing

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.910
the outcomes themselves without
developing the necessary

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:21.150
character needed to actually
reliably produce them.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:23.660
So to wrap this whole
thing up, just remember

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:26.540
this relationship between
building your character

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:27.930
and upgrading your life.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:30.270
If you focus on upgrading your character,

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:32.410
then the outcomes have a natural tendency

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:34.093
to take care of themselves.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:38.240
One of the best ways you
can invest in yourself

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:40.790
